{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/snapshottesting\/integratingwithtestframeworks"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/IntegratingWithTestFrameworks"},"kind":"article","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting"]]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Essentials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/assertSnapshot(of:as:named:options:fileID:file:testName:line:column:)","doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/SnapshotAssertionOptions","doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/MigrationGuides"],"title":"Essentials","generated":true}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"SnapshotTesting"}],"title":"Integrating with test frameworks"},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Learn how to use snapshot testing in the two main testing frameworks: Xcode’s XCTest and Swift’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"native testing framework."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Apple ecosystem currently has two primary testing frameworks, and unfortunately they are not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"compatible with each other. There is the XCTest framework, which is a private framework provided"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by Apple and heavily integrated into Xcode. And now there is Swift Testing, an open source testing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"framework built in Swift that is capable of integrating into a variety of environments."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"These two frameworks are not compatible in the sense that an assertion made in one framework"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from a test in the other framework will not trigger a test failure. So, if you are writing a test"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with the new "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Test"},{"type":"text","text":" macro style, and you use a test helper that ultimately calls "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"XCTFail"},{"type":"text","text":" under"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the hood, that will not bubble up to an actual test failure when tests are run. And similarly, if"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"you have a test case inheriting from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"XCTestCase"},{"type":"text","text":" that ultimiately invokes the new style "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#expect"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"macro, that too will not actually trigger a test failure."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"However, these details have all been hidden away in the SnapshotTesting library. You can simply"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"use "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/assertSnapshot(of:as:named:options:fileID:file:testName:line:column:)"},{"type":"text","text":" in either an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"XCTestCase"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"subclass "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"or"}]},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Test"},{"type":"text","text":", and it will dynamically detect what context it is running in and trigger"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the correct test failure:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["@Test ","func testFeature() {","  assertSnapshot(of: MyView(), as: .image)  \/\/ ✅","}","","class FeatureTests: XCTestCase {","  func testFeature() {","    assertSnapshot(of: MyView(), as: .image)  \/\/ ✅","  }","}"]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Configuring-snapshots","text":"Configuring snapshots","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For the most part, asserting on snapshots works the same whether you are using XCTest or Swift"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Testing. There is one major difference, and that is how snapshot configuration works. There are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"two major ways snapshots can be configured: "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/SnapshotTestingConfiguration\/diffTool-swift.property"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/SnapshotTestingConfiguration\/record-swift.property"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"diffTool"},{"type":"text","text":" property allows you to customize how a command is printed to the test failure"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"message that allows you to quickly open a diff of two files, such as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"http:\/\/kaleidoscope.app"},{"type":"text","text":". The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"record"},{"type":"text","text":" property allows you to change the mode of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"assertion so that new snapshots are generated and saved to disk."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"These properties can be overridden for a scope of an operation using the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/withSnapshotTesting(record:diffTool:snapshotNaming:referenceStorage:locale:timeZone:calendar:operation:)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"function. In a Swift Testing context"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"you can apply the "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/Testing\/Trait\/snapshots"},{"type":"text","text":" trait to either a single test or an entire suite:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import SnapshotTesting","","@Suite(.snapshots(record: .failed, diffTool: .ksdiff))","struct FeatureTests {","  …","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This will override the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"diffTool"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"record"},{"type":"text","text":" properties for each test in the suite."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In an XCTest context, the simplest way to do this is to override the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"invokeTest"},{"type":"text","text":" method on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"XCTestCase"},{"type":"text","text":" and wrap it in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withSnapshotTesting"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["class FeatureTests: XCTestCase {","  override func invokeTest() {","    withSnapshotTesting(record: .failed, diffTool: .ksdiff) {","      super.invokeTest()","    }","  }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This will override the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"diffTool"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"record"},{"type":"text","text":" properties for each test function."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"UI-Testing","text":"UI Testing","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Xcode’s UI testing tools are currently incompatible with Swift Testing. Simply adding"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Testing"},{"type":"text","text":" to any UI test target file will cause a compilation error saying that “Testing”"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"cannot be found. This complicates using SnapshotTesting in UI test targets because it needs to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"import Testing in order to provide the test helpers mentioned above."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The way in which Xcode disallows importing Testing in UI test targets is via the presence of a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"special Swift flag:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["-module_alias Testing=_Testing_Unavailable"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This is done so that people do not expect "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#expect"},{"type":"text","text":" and other Testing tools to work in UI test"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"targets. If you want to use SnapshotTesting in a UI test target, we recommend that you remove"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"this flag:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Open your project’s settings and navigate to the settings for your UI testing target.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Search for “Other Swift flags” in the “Build Settings” tab.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Delete the ","type":"text"},{"code":"$(inherited)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" flag.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Now you can "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import SnapshotTesting"},{"type":"text","text":" in UI test targets "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"and"}]},{"type":"text","text":" make use of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"assertSnapshot"},{"type":"text","text":". But"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"do remember that you "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"cannot"}]},{"type":"text","text":" use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#expect"},{"type":"text","text":" or any of the other tools from Swift Testing."}]}]}],"references":{"doc://SnapshotTesting/documentation/SnapshotTesting/SnapshotTestingConfiguration/diffTool-swift.property":{"type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"diffTool"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"SnapshotTestingConfiguration","preciseIdentifier":"s:15SnapshotTesting0aB13ConfigurationV"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"DiffTool","preciseIdentifier":"s:15SnapshotTesting0aB13ConfigurationV8DiffToolV"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/SnapshotTestingConfiguration\/diffTool-swift.property","url":"\/documentation\/snapshottesting\/snapshottestingconfiguration\/difftool-swift.property","kind":"symbol","title":"diffTool","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The diff tool use to print helpful test failure messages."}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://SnapshotTesting/documentation/SnapshotTesting/assertSnapshot(of:as:named:options:fileID:file:testName:line:column:)":{"type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"assertSnapshot"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Value"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"of"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"attribute","text":"@autoclosure "},{"kind":"text","text":"() "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Value"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"as"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:15SnapshotTesting12SnapshottingV","text":"Snapshotting"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Value"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"some"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"Any"},{"kind":"text","text":">, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"named"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"options"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:15SnapshotTesting0A16AssertionOptionsV","text":"SnapshotAssertionOptions"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"fileID"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s12StaticStringV","text":"StaticString"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"file"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s12StaticStringV","text":"StaticString"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"testName"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"line"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Su","text":"UInt"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"column"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Su","text":"UInt"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/assertSnapshot(of:as:named:options:fileID:file:testName:line:column:)","url":"\/documentation\/snapshottesting\/assertsnapshot(of:as:named:options:fileid:file:testname:line:column:)","kind":"symbol","title":"assertSnapshot(of:as:named:options:fileID:file:testName:line:column:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Asserts that a given value matches a reference on disk."}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://SnapshotTesting/documentation/SnapshotTesti